###Block: Descriptions
Bane Bow.MOD	DESC:See Text
Blink (Improved).MOD	DESC:Same as blink but better control; see text.
Cloudwalkers.MOD	DESC:Clouds support creatures, allowing fight.
Recitation (CD).MOD	DESC:Allies gain +2 or +3 on attacks and saves, and enemies suffer -2.
Blessing of the Spirits.MOD	DESC:+2 to AC and saves, counter mind control, hedge out elementals and outsiders.
Chastise Spirits.MOD	DESC:The spirit shaman uses divine energy to damage hostile spirits (incorporeal undead, fey, elementals, astral creatures, creatures with the spirit subtype, spirit folk, telthors, and creatures created by dream sight or wood wose) for (CASTERLEVEL)d6 damage.
Detect Spirits.MOD	DESC:Reveals spirits within 60 ft. This includes incorporeal undead, fey, elementals, astral creatures, creatures with the spirit subtype, spirit folk, telthors, and creatures created by dream sight or wood wose.
Favored of the Spirits.MOD	DESC:Cures (min(CASTERLEVEL*10,150)) points of damage, all diseases and mental conditions. The spell triggers if the caster is reduced to 0 hit points or less.
Spirit Journey.MOD	DESC:Step into the spirit plane to travel rapidly.
Warding of the Spirits.MOD	DESC:+2 to AC and saves, counter mind control, hedge out elementals and outsiders in 10-ft. radius for (CASTERLEVEL*10) minutes.
Dragon Breath (Red Dragon or Gold Dragon).MOD	DESC:You choose a red or gold and mimic its breath weapon.
Summon Monster III (Elementals).MOD	DESC:This spell functions like summon monster I, except that you can summon one elemental from the 3rd-level list, 1d3 elementals of the same kind from the 2nd-level list, or 1d4+1 elementals of the same kind from the 1st-level list
Summon Monster V (Medium Elemental).MOD	DESC:This spell functions like summon monster I, except that you can summon one elemental from the 5th-level list, 1d3 elementals of the same kind from the 4th-level list, or 1d4+1 elementals of the same kind from a lower-level list
Summon Monster VI (Large Elemental).MOD	DESC:This spell functions like summon monster I, except that you can summon one elemental from the 6th-level list, 1d3 elementals of the same kind from the 5th-level list, or 1d4+1 elementals of the same kind from a lower-level list
Summon Monster VII (Huge Elemental).MOD	DESC:This spell functions like summon monster I, except that you can summon one elemental from the 7th-level list, 1d3 elementals of the same kind from the 6th-level list, or 1d4+1 elementals of the same kind from a lower-level list
Summon Monster VIII (Greater Elemental).MOD	DESC:This spell functions like summon monster I, except that you can summon one elemental from the 8th-level list, 1d3 elementals of the same kind from the 7th-level list, or 1d4+1 elementals of the same kind from a lower-level list
Summon Monster IX (Elder Elemental).MOD	DESC:This spell functions like summon monster I, except that you can summon one elemental from the 9th-level list, 1d3 elementals of the same kind from the 8th-level list, or 1d4+1 elementals of the same kind from a lower-level list
Summon Nature's Ally V (Large Air Elemental).MOD	DESC:This spell functions like summon nature's ally I, except that you can summon one large air elemental from the 5th-level list.

